1
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:33,783
I'm driving.

2
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:35,952
I... You promised.

3
00:00:36,577 --> 00:00:37,870
- Yeah.
- Love you.

4
00:00:38,704 --> 00:00:39,747
Yeah, you do.

5
00:00:44,544 --> 00:00:45,586
Nobody move!

6
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,380
The keys!
Give me the keys!

7
00:00:48,005 --> 00:00:49,048
Step away from the car!

8
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:53,094
Get away from the car.

9
00:00:55,638 --> 00:00:56,681
Come on, baby.

10
00:00:58,683 --> 00:00:59,767
Go, baby, go!

11
00:01:00,476 --> 00:01:01,769
Buckle up!

12
00:01:49,275 --> 00:01:50,318
Hey!

13
00:01:51,277 --> 00:01:52,320
Hey, stop!

14
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:54,113
HPD! Stop!

15
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,243
Get off me!

16
00:01:59,702 --> 00:02:00,745
- Get Off me!
- Behind your back!

17
00:02:00,911 --> 00:02:01,954
Dispatch 42!

18
00:02:02,079 --> 00:02:04,290
- Female suspect in custody.
- Get off of me!

19
00:02:22,224 --> 00:02:23,309
Like butter, baby!

20
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:25,353
Let's celebrate.

21
00:02:31,233 --> 00:02:33,861
Where is she?
What happened?

22
00:02:34,403 --> 00:02:36,906
It was on the scanner,
cops chased her down.

23
00:02:39,450 --> 00:02:41,118
That's what happens
when you let a woman drive.

24
00:02:42,161 --> 00:02:43,329
What are you smiling about?

25
00:02:44,038 --> 00:02:45,081
Cole, I just...

26
00:02:54,674 --> 00:02:56,342
Go get a chamois.
Come buff this out.

27
00:02:56,967 --> 00:02:58,177
We should get out of town.

28
00:02:59,387 --> 00:03:01,430
We can't get out of town.
We've still got product to move.

29
00:03:01,597 --> 00:03:03,557
- We still need a car.
- What if she talks?

30
00:03:06,977 --> 00:03:08,187
You don't know Marie.

31
00:03:12,441 --> 00:03:14,318
"Armed robbery,
assault with a deadly weapon"

32
00:03:14,443 --> 00:03:17,905
"resisting arrest, felony eluding,
reckless driving."

33
00:03:18,614 --> 00:03:20,408
You know,
a cruel man would tack on

34
00:03:20,616 --> 00:03:22,368
running through
a red light and speeding

35
00:03:22,493 --> 00:03:24,370
but I'm not a cruel man.

36
00:03:26,789 --> 00:03:27,915
FBI, huh?

37
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,293
Didn't know I, uh,
rated the Feds.

38
00:03:31,419 --> 00:03:34,380
Your boyfriend, Cole Foster
runs a luxury-car-theft ring

39
00:03:34,797 --> 00:03:36,090
with jobs from Phoenix to Tulsa.

40
00:03:36,215 --> 00:03:37,967
Crossing state lines
makes it federal.

41
00:03:38,342 --> 00:03:41,220
- How old are you, Marie?
- Who cares?

42
00:03:42,346 --> 00:03:43,639
You have a lot of life left.

43
00:03:43,764 --> 00:03:45,307
I know you don't want
to throw it away.

44
00:03:45,599 --> 00:03:46,642
Under federal law

45
00:03:46,767 --> 00:03:48,394
we can charge you with being
your boyfriend's co-conspirator.

46
00:03:48,519 --> 00:03:49,562
You know what that means?

47
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:52,398
That means you answer for what
you did and anything he did.

48
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:55,234
And you can get
50 to 60 years, easy.

49
00:03:56,193 --> 00:03:58,070
You don't wanna walk
out of prison at 80.

50
00:03:59,029 --> 00:04:03,367
So help us, and we'll make
this mess go away a lot faster.

51
00:04:03,993 --> 00:04:05,411
Tell us where Cole is.

52
00:04:07,747 --> 00:04:09,039
You bastards.

53
00:04:10,249 --> 00:04:13,043
I'd go to hell for Cole.
You think I care about jail?

54
00:04:15,963 --> 00:04:17,006
Lock me up.

55
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:22,887
Take her.

56
00:04:27,683 --> 00:04:30,895
- Plan B?
- Plan B.

57
00:04:32,021 --> 00:04:33,898
Don't tell a whole lot
of little lies.

58
00:04:34,023 --> 00:04:36,108
Just one big lie is enough

59
00:04:36,233 --> 00:04:37,610
and everything else
just stays the same

60
00:04:37,735 --> 00:04:39,779
you're from Chicago
you got three brothers

61
00:04:39,987 --> 00:04:41,614
- you're ticklish.
- I am not ticklish.

62
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:43,824
- Yes, you are.
- Everybody is ticklish

63
00:04:43,949 --> 00:04:45,201
when they're being tickled.

64
00:04:45,367 --> 00:04:47,703
If you want someone to trust
you, ask them for a favor

65
00:04:48,037 --> 00:04:50,414
- even a small one.
- Jane, I know what I'm doing.

66
00:04:50,706 --> 00:04:51,749
One last thing.

67
00:04:52,750 --> 00:04:55,169
When you shower,
promise me this

68
00:04:55,836 --> 00:04:57,421
that you will wear
the flip-flops, please.

69
00:04:57,546 --> 00:05:00,549
A, it makes you look less attractive
which should be considered

70
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,843
and B,
the floor is a Petri dish.

71
00:05:03,135 --> 00:05:04,178
- Okay.
- Okay.

72
00:05:04,303 --> 00:05:05,721
- I hear you.
- Thank you.

73
00:05:06,472 --> 00:05:08,182
It's time.
Are you good?

74
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:10,392
Yeah.

75
00:05:13,354 --> 00:05:16,440
The warden has set it up so that you
will be sharing a cell with Marie.

76
00:05:17,149 --> 00:05:19,360
The sooner you get her to tell you
where Cole is, the better.

77
00:05:20,277 --> 00:05:21,320
I'm ready.

78
00:05:23,322 --> 00:05:24,490
Be careful, huh?

79
00:05:31,497 --> 00:05:35,125
- I'll wait for you.
- Hush. Go!

80
00:06:22,337 --> 00:06:24,631
{\an8}"McGregor, Teresa.
Transfer from Amarillo"

81
00:06:24,756 --> 00:06:27,467
{\an8}"prisoner number 90026, correct?"

82
00:06:32,764 --> 00:06:35,851
{\an8}We don't tolerate gangs,
drugs, or violence.

83
00:06:36,310 --> 00:06:38,020
{\an8}You violate the rules
and you will be transferred

84
00:06:38,145 --> 00:06:39,980
{\an8}to a higher-security institution.

85
00:06:40,731 --> 00:06:43,483
{\an8}Keep to the straight and narrow,
and we'll all get along fine.

86
00:06:44,192 --> 00:06:45,235
{\an8}This is you.

87
00:06:52,868 --> 00:06:53,911
{\an8}Hey.

88
00:06:57,623 --> 00:06:59,833
{\an8}I'm Teresa McGregor.
I'm your new bunkmate.

89
00:07:09,968 --> 00:07:12,137
{\an8}- What are you in for?
- Burglary.

90
00:07:12,971 --> 00:07:14,640
{\an8}Judge wouldn't give bail
for repeat offenders

91
00:07:14,765 --> 00:07:15,807
{\an8}so here I am.

92
00:07:17,142 --> 00:07:19,770
{\an8}- You?
- Grand Theft Auto.

93
00:07:20,854 --> 00:07:24,066
{\an8}Well, that's what they're charging me with
and like a million other things.

94
00:07:26,401 --> 00:07:27,444
{\an8}McGregor.

95
00:07:28,528 --> 00:07:32,240
{\an8}- That's Irish, huh?
- My grandparents came over from Derry.

96
00:07:34,493 --> 00:07:35,535
{\an8}Marie Flanagan.

97
00:07:35,953 --> 00:07:40,248
{\an8}Uh, mine were from
somewhere like that.

98
00:07:40,958 --> 00:07:42,000
I don't... I don't know.

99
00:07:43,710 --> 00:07:46,630
{\an8}Uh, you mind if I take the top bunk?
I get a little claustrophobic.

100
00:07:49,424 --> 00:07:51,885
Well, that depends, are you crazy
enough to take it from me?

101
00:07:54,179 --> 00:07:55,222
Forget it.

102
00:07:58,225 --> 00:07:59,393
{\an8}What I thought.

103
00:08:06,233 --> 00:08:07,401
Whoa. Whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa.

104
00:08:07,901 --> 00:08:08,944
What do you got there?

105
00:08:09,277 --> 00:08:11,697
- Coffee. Why?
- That's Jane's cup.

106
00:08:12,406 --> 00:08:14,574
- Seriously?
- Well, it's a rookie mistake no problem.

107
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:17,411
Just wash it, put it back
and he'll never know.

108
00:08:19,746 --> 00:08:20,998
Well, he, he might not know.

109
00:08:23,542 --> 00:08:25,794
- Okay. Sure.
- Yeah.

110
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:29,589
Hey, any idea who that is?

111
00:08:30,007 --> 00:08:31,091
She was here
a few days ago.

112
00:08:31,383 --> 00:08:33,260
Uh, her name's Cass,
I think.

113
00:08:33,385 --> 00:08:35,762
Abbot said she's with the CIA.
Don't know what she's here for.

114
00:08:36,013 --> 00:08:37,180
No, no, seriously, you...

115
00:08:37,305 --> 00:08:38,682
- You wanna wash that.
- Okay.

116
00:08:41,309 --> 00:08:44,229
- Your agent inside already?
- She's sharing a cell with Flanagan.

117
00:08:45,272 --> 00:08:49,151
The plan is for Lisbon to get Marie
to give up Cole Foster's location.

118
00:08:50,068 --> 00:08:51,361
I just hope
it doesn't take long.

119
00:08:52,362 --> 00:08:53,405
I know it's risky.

120
00:08:53,655 --> 00:08:56,033
The Agency appreciates everything
your people are doing.

121
00:08:56,158 --> 00:08:59,244
Ms. Cass, I'm all about
interagency cooperation

122
00:09:00,037 --> 00:09:01,079
it's great.

123
00:09:01,705 --> 00:09:04,833
But thanks to you
I put one of my best people in danger

124
00:09:05,292 --> 00:09:06,501
to catch a car thief

125
00:09:07,419 --> 00:09:10,130
and I don't know why the CIA
cares so damn much.

126
00:09:12,257 --> 00:09:13,383
Between us?

127
00:09:14,885 --> 00:09:15,927
Sure.

128
00:09:17,054 --> 00:09:19,848
Foster sells
the cars he steals overseas.

129
00:09:20,057 --> 00:09:22,517
His buyers are in
the Middle East, Europe.

130
00:09:23,143 --> 00:09:25,270
So he's plugged in
to international smugglers.

131
00:09:26,229 --> 00:09:29,024
People who smuggle luxury cars
can smuggle other things

132
00:09:29,357 --> 00:09:31,818
drugs, money, bombs.

133
00:09:31,985 --> 00:09:33,445
So you think
he's tied to terrorists.

134
00:09:33,779 --> 00:09:35,572
I think the people
he works with are

135
00:09:35,989 --> 00:09:37,407
and if you can get him
into custody

136
00:09:37,783 --> 00:09:39,076
we can have those names.

137
00:09:40,327 --> 00:09:41,536
Why go after him now?

138
00:09:42,871 --> 00:09:44,289
The NSA has picked up
some chatter

139
00:09:44,414 --> 00:09:47,375
about plans for
an operation here in the U.S.

140
00:09:47,709 --> 00:09:49,878
We think one of Foster's
contacts is in on it

141
00:09:50,003 --> 00:09:51,254
and it's coming soon.

142
00:09:51,797 --> 00:09:55,175
Now, I appreciate
that your agent is in danger

143
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:56,927
but I would think
that you would agree

144
00:09:57,719 --> 00:09:59,471
it's worth the risk.

145
00:10:07,604 --> 00:10:08,772
What's the CIA have to say?

146
00:10:09,272 --> 00:10:11,942
Well, nothing worth repeating.
What's that?

147
00:10:12,150 --> 00:10:14,653
It's a map Wylie made for me.

148
00:10:14,778 --> 00:10:16,738
Uh, this is Marie's route
during her car chase.

149
00:10:16,863 --> 00:10:18,281
You notice how she turns
that way, then that way

150
00:10:18,406 --> 00:10:21,660
- then that way again?
- Huh. So?

151
00:10:22,077 --> 00:10:23,787
Well, when you're being chased

152
00:10:23,912 --> 00:10:26,248
your subconscious
wants you to run home

153
00:10:26,373 --> 00:10:27,582
but your conscious mind

154
00:10:27,707 --> 00:10:29,209
doesn't want to lead
your pursuers there.

155
00:10:29,334 --> 00:10:31,419
So, she has, uh...

156
00:10:31,753 --> 00:10:33,130
Zigzagged in a way.

157
00:10:33,380 --> 00:10:35,924
But where she really wanted
to go was this neighborhood.

158
00:10:36,383 --> 00:10:38,051
That makes sense,
industrial area.

159
00:10:38,176 --> 00:10:40,971
Economic downturn hit it hard,
lots of empty warehouses.

160
00:10:41,263 --> 00:10:43,348
Just the place to hide
a lot of stolen cars.

161
00:10:43,807 --> 00:10:45,517
Well, if we find
Cole's base there

162
00:10:45,642 --> 00:10:46,768
we might be able
to scoop him up.

163
00:10:46,893 --> 00:10:47,936
Yeah, but that's
four square miles.

164
00:10:48,061 --> 00:10:49,437
We need a little bit more
to go on.

165
00:10:51,523 --> 00:10:52,607
Well, which warehouse
is it?

166
00:10:55,068 --> 00:10:56,778
Well, I can't do everything.

167
00:10:58,071 --> 00:11:00,824
Oh. Well, uh, let's see
if we can narrow it down.

168
00:11:01,116 --> 00:11:02,159
You got it.

169
00:11:04,911 --> 00:11:08,373
You're wearing a new aftershave.
I believe it has Ambergris in it.

170
00:11:08,498 --> 00:11:09,958
That's very expensive
for the office.

171
00:11:10,083 --> 00:11:11,668
What's the special occasion?

172
00:11:11,793 --> 00:11:13,503
- You know, date night with the wife.
- Nice.

173
00:11:13,753 --> 00:11:15,964
Yeah, Lena's on a short list
for a position

174
00:11:16,089 --> 00:11:17,924
in the commerce department
in D.C. so we're celebrating.

175
00:11:18,175 --> 00:11:19,843
Well, tell her congratulations for me.

176
00:11:20,177 --> 00:11:23,138
Oh, well, it's not said
and done yet, but we're hopeful.

177
00:11:26,057 --> 00:11:27,142
You know, Jane.

178
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:30,645
We will bring Lisbon
back home safe.

179
00:11:31,271 --> 00:11:32,314
Of course we will.

180
00:11:33,523 --> 00:11:34,566
Okay.

181
00:12:05,263 --> 00:12:06,973
- "What's your problem?"
- "Yeah, I don't like you."

182
00:12:07,098 --> 00:12:08,183
"I don't really care!"

183
00:12:08,308 --> 00:12:09,476
"Excuse me.
I'm gonna use the phone."

184
00:12:09,601 --> 00:12:10,769
"Yeah, you're gonna get in line
like the rest of us."

185
00:12:10,894 --> 00:12:12,229
- "I was in line!"
- "Oh, really?"

186
00:12:12,437 --> 00:12:14,856
"Yeah. You can't tell because you're
so busy looking at your own stupid..."

187
00:12:14,981 --> 00:12:16,441
"Hey, watch it, watch it."

188
00:12:16,775 --> 00:12:18,985
- "What, I wasn't even talking to you!"
- "Back off!"

189
00:12:19,110 --> 00:12:20,695
"You think you're too good to stand
in line or something?"

190
00:12:20,820 --> 00:12:22,948
You've been eyeballing me
since I walked through that door.

191
00:12:23,114 --> 00:12:24,741
- What's going on?
- Yo, mind your business!

192
00:12:24,866 --> 00:12:25,909
- Stay out of it.
- Hey.

193
00:12:27,369 --> 00:12:28,411
Cut it out.

194
00:12:29,246 --> 00:12:30,664
I'm not trying
to pick a fight.

195
00:12:30,789 --> 00:12:33,541
Bitch, who the hell
are you?

196
00:12:33,792 --> 00:12:35,418
Somebody who doesn't
want to get transferred

197
00:12:35,543 --> 00:12:37,212
to higher security
just like you.

198
00:12:37,462 --> 00:12:38,505
Oh, yeah?

199
00:12:39,965 --> 00:12:41,216
We're gonna go back
to our bunk

200
00:12:41,341 --> 00:12:44,261
and you're gonna get back
in line and make a phone call.

201
00:12:48,139 --> 00:12:49,474
Hey. Phone's open.

202
00:12:50,350 --> 00:12:51,685
I'm gonna call my old man.

203
00:12:52,978 --> 00:12:55,021
Yeah. Whatever.

204
00:12:56,231 --> 00:12:57,899
Oh, and I'll see you around.

205
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:08,034
- What the hell was that?
- I raised three brothers.

206
00:13:08,159 --> 00:13:09,286
You learn to deal with aggression.

207
00:13:09,411 --> 00:13:12,163
Well, I didn't need your help, all right?
I can handle myself.

208
00:13:14,582 --> 00:13:15,625
How you holding up?

209
00:13:16,334 --> 00:13:17,377
"Roommate troubles?"

210
00:13:18,086 --> 00:13:19,379
It's like we're doing the cha-cha.

211
00:13:19,713 --> 00:13:22,132
"I take one step forward,
she takes one step back."

212
00:13:22,632 --> 00:13:23,675
Does she have any friends?

213
00:13:23,967 --> 00:13:26,845
She likes picking fights
a little bit too much, a loner.

214
00:13:27,262 --> 00:13:28,638
"Oh, well, she needs a friend."

215
00:13:29,347 --> 00:13:30,390
We all do.

216
00:13:31,891 --> 00:13:34,853
- You have not met this girl.
- Oh, a tough cookie

217
00:13:34,978 --> 00:13:37,188
likes to hide her emotions
under a hard veneer?

218
00:13:38,523 --> 00:13:39,566
Yeah.

219
00:13:40,317 --> 00:13:42,986
Yeah, I think I've met
a woman like that before.

220
00:13:44,821 --> 00:13:45,864
Is that so?

221
00:13:46,614 --> 00:13:48,908
Uh, you, you wanna know how I got
her to lower her guard?

222
00:13:49,909 --> 00:13:50,952
How?

223
00:13:51,828 --> 00:13:54,039
Uh, I lowered my own.

224
00:14:03,381 --> 00:14:04,424
Marie.

225
00:14:09,804 --> 00:14:11,973
- Marie.
- What?

226
00:14:12,682 --> 00:14:13,933
I can't sleep.

227
00:14:14,726 --> 00:14:18,063
- You?
- No. It's too hot.

228
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:19,522
Yeah.

229
00:14:21,316 --> 00:14:22,901
I miss my boyfriend.

230
00:14:25,653 --> 00:14:26,863
What's he do?

231
00:14:28,865 --> 00:14:29,991
He's a hustler.

232
00:14:31,868 --> 00:14:33,828
He uses his brains
to get by.

233
00:14:34,287 --> 00:14:36,748
Like a con artist?
That's cool.

234
00:14:39,292 --> 00:14:40,418
How long you been together?

235
00:14:41,169 --> 00:14:44,798
We've known each other
a long time, years and years

236
00:14:44,964 --> 00:14:46,591
but we weren't together.

237
00:14:46,883 --> 00:14:49,010
I mean, we,
we were friends, but...

238
00:14:50,387 --> 00:14:53,223
I couldn't admit that my feelings
had changed for him

239
00:14:54,599 --> 00:14:55,767
not even to myself.

240
00:14:58,603 --> 00:14:59,979
I know what that's like.

241
00:15:02,524 --> 00:15:06,486
I tried to run away.
I met a nice guy.

242
00:15:06,653 --> 00:15:09,739
He was a good man
but not the right man.

243
00:15:11,658 --> 00:15:13,284
I was gonna marry him.

244
00:15:14,369 --> 00:15:16,538
Then Patrick told me
he loved me

245
00:15:16,663 --> 00:15:19,040
and that he didn't
want me to leave.

246
00:15:20,417 --> 00:15:23,461
- What'd you do?
- I stayed.

247
00:15:25,630 --> 00:15:28,716
It felt so good
not to live a lie anymore.

248
00:15:30,093 --> 00:15:31,219
Scary, too.

249
00:15:32,387 --> 00:15:33,513
I don't know
what's gonna happen

250
00:15:33,638 --> 00:15:35,682
you know, if he's gonna
stick around or...

251
00:15:43,523 --> 00:15:46,985
My boyfriend,
his name's Cole.

252
00:15:48,069 --> 00:15:49,612
He's a real outlaw.

253
00:15:52,198 --> 00:15:53,491
I like that.

254
00:15:54,701 --> 00:15:56,870
Cole and me, we live wild.

255
00:15:57,412 --> 00:16:01,207
I mean, it's like wild.

256
00:16:02,333 --> 00:16:04,335
Like, right now,
we're living in a warehouse.

257
00:16:04,669 --> 00:16:06,129
You live in a warehouse?

258
00:16:06,337 --> 00:16:07,755
It's actually more like a hideout.

259
00:16:08,214 --> 00:16:10,008
Cars like
you wouldn't believe

260
00:16:10,258 --> 00:16:12,677
million-dollar cars,
expensive stuff

261
00:16:13,803 --> 00:16:16,848
but we live off of
gas station chimichangas. It's...

262
00:16:17,891 --> 00:16:18,933
It's wild.

263
00:16:19,350 --> 00:16:22,145
Wild is one thing,
no shower is another.

264
00:16:22,437 --> 00:16:24,147
Aw, hell, we have a shower.

265
00:16:24,981 --> 00:16:28,318
Cole even stole cable from
the no-tell motel down the block.

266
00:16:36,534 --> 00:16:37,744
I hear we caught a break.

267
00:16:38,620 --> 00:16:39,787
Yeah, Lisbon called in.

268
00:16:39,954 --> 00:16:42,081
Marie told her about a warehouse
she and Cole stay in.

269
00:16:42,499 --> 00:16:44,459
- Did she give a location?
- Not an address

270
00:16:44,584 --> 00:16:46,294
but looking in the neighborhood
Jane pinpointed

271
00:16:46,419 --> 00:16:48,546
we found a warehouse that fit
all the details Marie gave us

272
00:16:48,671 --> 00:16:51,049
down to the
gas station chimichangas.

273
00:16:51,758 --> 00:16:52,842
Chimichangas?

274
00:16:53,218 --> 00:16:54,802
Yeah, well, that...
That's not important.

275
00:16:54,928 --> 00:16:56,095
What is important
is that the warehouse

276
00:16:56,221 --> 00:16:58,014
is leased by a fake corporation.

277
00:16:58,306 --> 00:16:59,599
Sounds like
what we're looking for.

278
00:16:59,849 --> 00:17:01,142
Well, it's enough for a warrant.

279
00:17:01,392 --> 00:17:02,936
Why don't you get a team together
and head down there

280
00:17:03,061 --> 00:17:04,187
and see what you can find?

281
00:17:09,150 --> 00:17:11,194
That's a load of crap, man.
You got nothing on me.

282
00:17:11,361 --> 00:17:12,529
You're gonna be hearing
from my lawyer.

283
00:17:12,654 --> 00:17:14,948
We just caught you in a warehouse
full of stolen vehicles.

284
00:17:15,907 --> 00:17:17,325
You're the one that should be trying
to make a deal with me.

285
00:17:17,450 --> 00:17:18,493
If you're too stupid to see that

286
00:17:18,618 --> 00:17:20,495
I don't know what value you have
for the FBI.

287
00:17:20,662 --> 00:17:22,997
Uh, come on, man.
Let's... Let's talk.

288
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:32,549
Do you wanna tell me
where Cole Foster is?

289
00:17:33,675 --> 00:17:36,219
Look, his old lady
got caught last week.

290
00:17:36,761 --> 00:17:37,929
It has him paranoid as hell.

291
00:17:38,096 --> 00:17:39,764
He's in town.
That's all I know.

292
00:17:39,889 --> 00:17:41,808
If he's so paranoid,
why is he sticking around?

293
00:17:42,892 --> 00:17:43,935
Good question.

294
00:17:44,686 --> 00:17:45,728
Tell me
how I can find him.

295
00:17:47,397 --> 00:17:48,940
Man, I don't even have
his burner number.

296
00:17:49,732 --> 00:17:51,859
Hendricks is the only one that
knows how to get a hold of him.

297
00:17:55,488 --> 00:17:56,531
Ronald Hendricks?

298
00:17:59,576 --> 00:18:00,618
That's right.

299
00:18:02,579 --> 00:18:03,788
"And how can I find Hendricks?"

300
00:18:05,498 --> 00:18:07,000
"I don't know. He's with Cole I guess."

301
00:18:10,461 --> 00:18:12,171
We already put a BOLO
out on Hendricks.

302
00:18:12,297 --> 00:18:13,965
- That's a dead end.
- Maybe.

303
00:18:14,424 --> 00:18:16,801
Marie's useless as a source
of information now.

304
00:18:17,802 --> 00:18:18,845
Let's pull Lisbon out.

305
00:18:20,763 --> 00:18:22,849
Marie may be useless
as a source of information

306
00:18:22,974 --> 00:18:25,226
- but she still has a use.
- What's that?

307
00:18:25,351 --> 00:18:27,020
Well, Cole should leave town,
but he won't.

308
00:18:27,353 --> 00:18:29,188
It's obvious why,
he doesn't wanna leave Marie

309
00:18:29,314 --> 00:18:32,525
- so, we give her to him.
- How?

310
00:18:33,026 --> 00:18:34,902
We don't pull Lisbon
out of jail

311
00:18:35,903 --> 00:18:37,405
we break her out.

312
00:18:44,142 --> 00:18:47,562
- You wore a vest.
- Oh, this? This old thing?

313
00:18:47,896 --> 00:18:49,356
Well, I thought
I should look the part.

314
00:18:49,564 --> 00:18:50,607
I like it.

315
00:18:51,149 --> 00:18:54,444
Well, that's... That's good to know.
How are you?

316
00:18:55,654 --> 00:19:00,075
I'm fine. The food is not good.
I would kill for a salad.

317
00:19:03,078 --> 00:19:04,371
So, we didn't get him?

318
00:19:05,288 --> 00:19:06,331
What now?

319
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:09,834
You and Marie are gonna break out
of here and lead us to Cole.

320
00:19:10,335 --> 00:19:11,378
Okay.

321
00:19:11,628 --> 00:19:13,171
You're gonna provide
the breakout plan

322
00:19:13,463 --> 00:19:15,048
Marie is gonna provide the ride.

323
00:19:15,423 --> 00:19:17,092
And you think Cole's
gonna be waiting for her?

324
00:19:17,300 --> 00:19:19,135
Maybe. Or he'll be very close.

325
00:19:21,137 --> 00:19:22,514
How are we
gonna break out?

326
00:19:22,847 --> 00:19:24,182
I'm working on a plan now.

327
00:19:24,391 --> 00:19:26,643
So I just say, Marie, we're gonna
bust out of this joint?

328
00:19:26,768 --> 00:19:28,687
It's not gonna be your idea,
it's gonna be her idea.

329
00:19:28,812 --> 00:19:30,564
Cousin Ricky
needs surgery again.

330
00:19:30,814 --> 00:19:31,856
He's got to lose
his gall bladder.

331
00:19:31,982 --> 00:19:33,358
- Doctor says it's got to go.
- Huh?

332
00:19:33,733 --> 00:19:35,527
Huh, what does it do?
What does a gall bladder do?

333
00:19:35,735 --> 00:19:37,737
I mean, can you even live
without a gall bladder?

334
00:19:39,614 --> 00:19:40,657
When she leaves that room

335
00:19:41,032 --> 00:19:44,327
breaking out will be
the only thing on her mind.

336
00:19:46,746 --> 00:19:47,789
Have a seat.

337
00:19:53,837 --> 00:19:55,005
Bite me.

338
00:19:57,924 --> 00:20:00,552
So, I guess that means
you haven't changed your mind

339
00:20:00,677 --> 00:20:02,929
about telling us
where Cole Foster is.

340
00:20:05,307 --> 00:20:06,349
Okay.

341
00:20:06,516 --> 00:20:09,686
Well, he can send you a postcard
when you get settled.

342
00:20:11,646 --> 00:20:13,273
What does that mean?

343
00:20:13,648 --> 00:20:16,026
That means I'm allowing
the Houston D.A.

344
00:20:16,151 --> 00:20:17,736
to file charges on you.

345
00:20:19,070 --> 00:20:20,864
You will be transferred
to Mountain View

346
00:20:20,989 --> 00:20:23,241
- while you await your trial.
- Mountain View?

347
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:25,493
That's a SuperMax.

348
00:20:25,702 --> 00:20:28,121
Well, it takes about 48 hours
for the paperwork to clear

349
00:20:28,246 --> 00:20:29,289
if you wanna get packed.

350
00:20:29,748 --> 00:20:32,792
Uh, no way.

351
00:20:33,335 --> 00:20:34,711
Mountain View's for crazies.

352
00:20:34,836 --> 00:20:36,838
Well, it's a more
structured environment

353
00:20:37,797 --> 00:20:39,674
23 hours a day in your cell

354
00:20:40,717 --> 00:20:42,886
- constant supervision.
- You can't do that.

355
00:20:44,179 --> 00:20:45,930
- You can't.
- I can!

356
00:20:46,681 --> 00:20:49,559
So you enjoy your time here
for the next 48 hours

357
00:20:49,726 --> 00:20:53,188
because it is the best
it's gonna get for a long time.

358
00:21:14,125 --> 00:21:15,293
SuperMax.

359
00:21:16,628 --> 00:21:18,338
I hear you don't even
get out of your cell to shower

360
00:21:18,463 --> 00:21:20,548
they just roll one up
to the door.

361
00:21:20,882 --> 00:21:24,260
I just... I won't go. I won't.

362
00:21:24,636 --> 00:21:26,513
I won't, I won't, I won't go.

363
00:21:29,140 --> 00:21:30,934
That does not sound good.

364
00:21:33,603 --> 00:21:35,021
I got some bad news, too.

365
00:21:36,272 --> 00:21:37,857
The D.A.'s going after me.

366
00:21:38,692 --> 00:21:40,110
I'm a three-time loser.

367
00:21:40,777 --> 00:21:43,446
I'm facing 25 to life.
I can't do it.

368
00:21:44,030 --> 00:21:45,156
Damn pigs.

369
00:21:46,408 --> 00:21:48,743
I'm so sick of getting
pushed around. It's...

370
00:21:50,912 --> 00:21:53,415
I just wish there was
something we could do.

371
00:21:53,623 --> 00:21:55,458
We... Just get out of here.

372
00:21:57,001 --> 00:21:58,420
Like break out?

373
00:21:59,629 --> 00:22:00,672
Yeah.

374
00:22:01,840 --> 00:22:04,300
I guess. It's easier to get out of here
than Mountain View.

375
00:22:07,721 --> 00:22:08,763
Hey.

376
00:22:09,389 --> 00:22:11,099
You've done break-ins
before, right?

377
00:22:12,142 --> 00:22:13,476
How hard can a breakout be?

378
00:22:14,185 --> 00:22:15,228
Hard.

379
00:22:16,312 --> 00:22:17,689
But that doesn't mean
it's impossible.

380
00:22:18,314 --> 00:22:21,067
But you can figure it out, right?
You got brains. I can tell.

381
00:22:21,651 --> 00:22:22,694
Maybe.

382
00:22:22,819 --> 00:22:24,362
But if I get us on
the other side of that wall

383
00:22:24,487 --> 00:22:26,322
someone's got to get us
out of state right away.

384
00:22:26,448 --> 00:22:28,450
Otherwise, the cops
will just pick us up.

385
00:22:28,950 --> 00:22:30,952
My man can get us
anywhere we wanna go.

386
00:22:31,703 --> 00:22:32,746
Where do you wanna be?

387
00:22:33,663 --> 00:22:36,249
Patrick's in Florida.
I could go see him.

388
00:22:37,834 --> 00:22:39,961
I'm not gonna rot
in a SuperMax.

389
00:22:42,172 --> 00:22:43,256
I say we do it.

390
00:22:44,257 --> 00:22:45,300
I'm in.

391
00:22:49,095 --> 00:22:50,305
I'm gonna make a phone call.

392
00:22:51,598 --> 00:22:53,224
I knew I liked you.

393
00:23:00,231 --> 00:23:02,984
No. Listen. No, Mark,
listen to me for a second.

394
00:23:03,318 --> 00:23:04,360
Will you listen?

395
00:23:04,652 --> 00:23:07,113
I swear you have nothing
between your ears but wax.

396
00:23:07,489 --> 00:23:09,324
You're my brother
and I love you

397
00:23:09,449 --> 00:23:10,825
but you are dumber
than a sack of rocks.

398
00:23:10,950 --> 00:23:13,453
"Now, will you just calm down
and listen for a minute?"

399
00:23:13,828 --> 00:23:15,246
This one's angry
at her brother.

400
00:23:16,080 --> 00:23:18,792
- It's not Marie.
- She's call before lights-out.

401
00:23:20,126 --> 00:23:21,169
New call.

402
00:23:22,754 --> 00:23:25,882
She wants to know
who's feeding Taco, her cat.

403
00:23:27,634 --> 00:23:28,676
I hope someone is.

404
00:23:28,968 --> 00:23:30,595
Don't we need warrants
to listen on phone calls?

405
00:23:30,762 --> 00:23:32,180
Not for jailhouse payphones.

406
00:23:32,972 --> 00:23:35,225
Her son is feeding Taco.
Taco is being fed.

407
00:23:35,642 --> 00:23:37,936
Good. New call.

408
00:23:39,896 --> 00:23:40,939
It's not Marie.

409
00:23:41,314 --> 00:23:42,774
You know, I used to date
a prisoner.

410
00:23:44,275 --> 00:23:45,902
- No, you didn't.
- Her name was Velma.

411
00:23:46,402 --> 00:23:47,445
Big Vel.

412
00:23:48,196 --> 00:23:49,656
- Big Vel?
- Mm-hm. Yep.

413
00:23:51,074 --> 00:23:53,117
And why did Big Vel
go to prison?

414
00:23:53,409 --> 00:23:54,619
Horse thief.

415
00:23:55,537 --> 00:23:56,579
Yeah, right.

416
00:23:58,665 --> 00:23:59,707
Well, I...

417
00:23:59,958 --> 00:24:02,210
- Wait, hold on. New call.
- "Hey."

418
00:24:02,627 --> 00:24:03,962
- I think it's her.
- "It's Marie."

419
00:24:04,379 --> 00:24:07,966
- Let me listen.
- "I got some news, big news."

420
00:24:08,633 --> 00:24:10,969
"The kids are coming home
from camp tomorrow."

421
00:24:12,178 --> 00:24:14,889
You need to pick up the kids
a little sooner than expected.

422
00:24:15,390 --> 00:24:16,724
"Right. I got it."

423
00:24:16,850 --> 00:24:18,184
- Is that Cole?
- I don't know.

424
00:24:19,644 --> 00:24:20,687
"When should I pick them up?"

425
00:24:21,729 --> 00:24:23,064
I'll be in touch again soon.

426
00:24:23,731 --> 00:24:24,774
"Be ready."

427
00:24:25,650 --> 00:24:26,818
Can we trace the call?

428
00:24:29,904 --> 00:24:30,989
No, she called a burner.

429
00:24:31,114 --> 00:24:33,199
No chance of tracking him down
from that.

430
00:24:35,952 --> 00:24:37,453
But now he'll come to us.

431
00:24:40,832 --> 00:24:42,542
It's time to plan a jailbreak.

432
00:24:45,712 --> 00:24:47,171
These are cameras.

433
00:24:47,297 --> 00:24:49,257
These are where
we'll find the COs.

434
00:24:49,382 --> 00:24:51,968
I've got maps of electric lines,
pipes, guard schedules.

435
00:24:52,218 --> 00:24:53,344
Well, the problem is simple.

436
00:24:53,553 --> 00:24:55,847
Lisbon and Marie
are inside the wall

437
00:24:56,014 --> 00:24:57,432
we need to get them
outside the wall.

438
00:24:57,682 --> 00:24:59,183
There's three ways
to get past a wall

439
00:24:59,309 --> 00:25:01,019
over, under, and through.

440
00:25:01,227 --> 00:25:02,353
Well, they don't
have time to tunnel.

441
00:25:02,687 --> 00:25:04,564
Sewage lines, if they can get
to the main drainage area?

442
00:25:04,731 --> 00:25:05,899
They'll need tools
to open it up.

443
00:25:06,065 --> 00:25:07,108
Can they go over the wall?

444
00:25:07,317 --> 00:25:08,359
What about the guard towers?

445
00:25:08,484 --> 00:25:11,029
See the southwest corner there?
Visibility's low.

446
00:25:11,154 --> 00:25:12,864
I mean, that section of wall
is 30 feet.

447
00:25:13,698 --> 00:25:15,825
- Grappling hooks?
- Grappling hooks?

448
00:25:16,910 --> 00:25:18,494
Seems to me
they should just go through.

449
00:25:18,786 --> 00:25:20,496
I mean, the people
that built this jail

450
00:25:20,663 --> 00:25:22,624
were nice enough
to put doors in the walls.

451
00:25:22,749 --> 00:25:23,917
Why don't they just use them?

452
00:25:24,125 --> 00:25:25,710
You see, there, that... That door.

453
00:25:25,877 --> 00:25:28,504
They should go
right through that door.

454
00:25:28,838 --> 00:25:31,841
They're gonna need a mop
and a bucket with a hole in it.

455
00:25:32,759 --> 00:25:34,344
"Okay, so they'll look
like they're cleaning."

456
00:25:34,761 --> 00:25:37,013
- "Why does the bucket need a hole?"
- "We'll get there."

457
00:25:37,639 --> 00:25:42,060
This door here is the key, not as
an escape route. It's a misdirect.

458
00:26:02,872 --> 00:26:05,583
"This is the boundary between
the guards' world and the prisoners'."

459
00:26:06,709 --> 00:26:09,879
"At shift change, it should be
empty except for the guard."

460
00:26:10,213 --> 00:26:13,174
"When the bucket empties,
it'll start a chain reaction."

461
00:26:14,217 --> 00:26:15,343
"A noisy one."

462
00:26:31,693 --> 00:26:35,071
If they're spotted in prison clothes
on that side of the line, game's over.

463
00:26:35,321 --> 00:26:37,824
Which is why they have to head
straight to the employees' locker room.

464
00:26:45,164 --> 00:26:46,749
And if they get there
just before shift change

465
00:26:46,874 --> 00:26:48,793
"they can leave with the cafeteria workers."

466
00:26:52,630 --> 00:26:53,965
What if someone thinks
they don't belong?

467
00:26:54,298 --> 00:26:56,426
The key to walking
in or out of any place

468
00:26:56,551 --> 00:26:57,885
is posture and momentum.

469
00:26:58,011 --> 00:26:59,387
"You just keep moving forward"

470
00:26:59,512 --> 00:27:00,888
"like you know exactly
where you're going."

471
00:27:01,222 --> 00:27:02,640
"People see
that kind of posture"

472
00:27:02,765 --> 00:27:04,225
"and they decide
that you belong there"

473
00:27:04,350 --> 00:27:06,728
"before their conscious brain
can even think about it."

474
00:27:07,687 --> 00:27:08,896
Then she's in your hands.

475
00:27:15,028 --> 00:27:16,070
That's Hendricks over there.

476
00:27:16,195 --> 00:27:18,281
He'll get us to Cole,
and Cole will take us out of state.

477
00:27:19,365 --> 00:27:20,408
Hey, there.

478
00:27:20,658 --> 00:27:22,618
- This your friend?
- Teresa, it's Hendricks.

479
00:27:22,785 --> 00:27:25,413
- Hey, Teresa.
- You keep your paws off her. She's taken.

480
00:27:35,965 --> 00:27:38,176
We're in position.
We have eyes on the car.

481
00:27:42,889 --> 00:27:45,600
Vega, Lisbon's car
has just pulled out.

482
00:27:50,188 --> 00:27:51,230
Not too close.

483
00:27:55,151 --> 00:27:56,819
"Cole is not inside.
Do you see them?"

484
00:27:57,028 --> 00:27:58,237
Don't worry.
The chopper's got them.

485
00:27:58,404 --> 00:28:00,448
I thought Cole would've picked
them up himself.

486
00:28:00,823 --> 00:28:03,493
No, he's thinking like a hunted
animal right now, he's hiding.

487
00:28:14,712 --> 00:28:16,380
"Hold on.
They're slowing down."

488
00:28:17,048 --> 00:28:18,257
"Not sure what they're doing."

489
00:28:26,265 --> 00:28:27,308
"Vega, be alert."

490
00:28:27,433 --> 00:28:30,311
We've just pulled into
a parking garage off Sunshine.

491
00:28:31,270 --> 00:28:32,939
The chopper can't see in here.
We're gonna lose her.

492
00:28:41,864 --> 00:28:43,116
Abbot, what is going on?

493
00:28:43,324 --> 00:28:45,076
They're switching cars.
I'm gonna go follow her.

494
00:28:46,828 --> 00:28:48,037
Watch the exit.

495
00:29:00,216 --> 00:29:03,052
Hey. You wanna go your own way,
that's up to you.

496
00:29:03,427 --> 00:29:06,097
I need a ride out of Texas.
That was the deal. Let's go.

497
00:29:20,444 --> 00:29:22,280
They switched vehicles.
There's no sign of Lisbon.

498
00:29:22,572 --> 00:29:24,407
Cho and I will traverse
the north and south streets

499
00:29:24,532 --> 00:29:25,575
a one-mile radius.

500
00:29:25,700 --> 00:29:26,868
"We'll get other teams
to help us search."

501
00:29:26,993 --> 00:29:29,078
You don't even know
what kind of car she's driving.

502
00:29:29,328 --> 00:29:30,538
How far is the garage?

503
00:29:30,913 --> 00:29:32,665
- Uh, from here, three miles.
- All right.

504
00:29:33,499 --> 00:29:36,085
They have to meet Cole someplace.
That gives us a little time.

505
00:29:36,419 --> 00:29:37,962
Let's go.
We're gonna join the search.

506
00:29:48,812 --> 00:29:50,147
Cole told me
to call from here.

507
00:29:50,689 --> 00:29:51,773
He'll let me know
where to meet him.

508
00:29:53,108 --> 00:29:54,234
Tell him to hurry up.

509
00:29:55,652 --> 00:29:56,695
- You hungry?
- Sure.

510
00:29:56,945 --> 00:29:58,780
Yeah, I'm starving.
Let's get something to eat.

511
00:30:02,201 --> 00:30:03,243
What?

512
00:30:03,744 --> 00:30:04,953
We just got out of jail.

513
00:30:05,829 --> 00:30:06,872
Oh, right.

514
00:30:10,667 --> 00:30:11,710
Hey.

515
00:30:18,300 --> 00:30:20,052
I'm gonna get
a big pile of cookies

516
00:30:20,761 --> 00:30:21,887
and candy

517
00:30:22,387 --> 00:30:24,306
and a soda big enough
to drown in.

518
00:30:24,932 --> 00:30:27,392
- What do you want?
- I think I'm just gonna get some water.

519
00:30:27,684 --> 00:30:31,146
Oh, look at this, chocolate.
That could be good.

520
00:30:32,564 --> 00:30:33,607
- These are...
- Hey!

521
00:30:38,820 --> 00:30:40,322
Hey, troublemaker.

522
00:30:41,156 --> 00:30:42,199
What are you doing?

523
00:30:42,741 --> 00:30:45,494
- What, is this your new BFF?
- Yes, this is Teresa McGregor.

524
00:30:45,619 --> 00:30:47,329
Teresa McGregor,
meet Cole.

525
00:30:48,413 --> 00:30:50,666
Teresa McGregor? I don't know her.
Why'd you bring her here?

526
00:30:50,832 --> 00:30:52,292
'Cause I promised her
a ride out of here.

527
00:30:52,501 --> 00:30:54,253
I didn't promise
Teresa McGregor a ride.

528
00:30:54,628 --> 00:30:55,796
Uh, this isn't charity.

529
00:30:55,963 --> 00:30:57,548
The breakout plan
was my idea.

530
00:30:58,757 --> 00:31:01,093
Come on, Cole!
She's good people, seriously.

531
00:31:01,468 --> 00:31:02,511
All right, good people.

532
00:31:02,803 --> 00:31:04,012
How do you feel about
getting out of Texas?

533
00:31:04,137 --> 00:31:05,931
- Sounds good to me.
- All right.

534
00:31:06,848 --> 00:31:09,101
Half a mile down that road
there's a helicopter

535
00:31:09,726 --> 00:31:11,144
- all fueled up, all right?
- Yeah?

536
00:31:11,311 --> 00:31:12,354
It'll get us past any dragnet

537
00:31:12,479 --> 00:31:13,855
they got set up for you
the two of you troublemakers.

538
00:31:14,106 --> 00:31:16,483
Wow. A helicopter? Since when
do you fly a helicopter?

539
00:31:16,608 --> 00:31:18,569
Hendricks flew them
in Afghanistan.

540
00:31:18,694 --> 00:31:20,028
Don't worry
your pretty little head.

541
00:31:20,153 --> 00:31:22,072
You two buy whatever you need to buy.
Let's get out of here.

542
00:31:22,197 --> 00:31:24,449
- I'm getting the sixer. Let's go.
- I'm just gonna grab some aspirin.

543
00:31:24,575 --> 00:31:25,659
- I have a headache.
- Okay.

544
00:31:32,624 --> 00:31:33,667
Hey.

545
00:31:34,543 --> 00:31:35,794
What are you typing
on that phone, man?

546
00:31:36,712 --> 00:31:39,089
- Excuse me?
- Let me check out your phone.

547
00:31:39,923 --> 00:31:41,550
Let me see your phone?
What are you hiding?

548
00:31:42,843 --> 00:31:44,678
Hey, man! What are you, crazy?
Back off!

549
00:31:44,970 --> 00:31:46,471
Do you want me to call the cops?

550
00:31:46,805 --> 00:31:47,848
Hey...

551
00:31:55,814 --> 00:31:56,857
Come here.

552
00:32:00,819 --> 00:32:02,863
Did you just see him
flop like that?

553
00:32:04,156 --> 00:32:06,283
Come here.
Come over!

554
00:32:09,828 --> 00:32:12,289
- You got a problem?
- No, I told you she's cool.

555
00:32:14,041 --> 00:32:15,876
No. No problem.

556
00:32:20,172 --> 00:32:23,216
All right, let's go!
Let's go, let's go, good people! Come on!

557
00:32:25,469 --> 00:32:26,928
Out of here!

558
00:32:47,658 --> 00:32:49,117
I need you two
to stay where you are.

559
00:32:49,743 --> 00:32:51,495
- This is a crime scene.
- Michelle Vega, FBI.

560
00:32:52,120 --> 00:32:53,872
We heard the shots fired call
over the scanner.

561
00:32:53,997 --> 00:32:56,249
We have reason to believe this could
be connected to a missing agent.

562
00:32:56,375 --> 00:32:58,085
- I need your assistance.
- Yes, ma'am.

563
00:32:58,460 --> 00:32:59,670
How long have you been
on the scene?

564
00:33:00,087 --> 00:33:01,296
Call came in
15 minutes ago.

565
00:33:01,588 --> 00:33:03,924
I've been here about a minute.
You guys got here fast.

566
00:33:05,592 --> 00:33:06,677
Get crime-scene tape up.

567
00:33:07,094 --> 00:33:09,388
Have any other responding
officers set up the perimeter.

568
00:33:10,222 --> 00:33:11,473
And check to see
if the security cameras

569
00:33:11,598 --> 00:33:13,600
- caught the crime on tape.
- Yes, ma'am.

570
00:33:17,479 --> 00:33:20,440
That's her.
That's Lisbon's footprint.

571
00:33:21,191 --> 00:33:23,360
So she's still with him.
That... that's good, right?

572
00:33:24,736 --> 00:33:27,114
Look at the angle her foot is.
It's like she's pointing.

573
00:33:27,239 --> 00:33:29,866
She's, she's pointing us
that direction.

574
00:33:29,991 --> 00:33:31,201
Or she stepped in it by accident.

575
00:33:31,618 --> 00:33:33,662
No, she would never do that.
Let's... Let's go.

576
00:33:33,787 --> 00:33:36,540
Okay, Jane, we don't know where they are.
There's protocol here.

577
00:33:36,873 --> 00:33:39,876
I'll call Abbott, explain the situation
see if he and Cho are close.

578
00:33:40,001 --> 00:33:41,336
You call whoever
you need to call, yeah.

579
00:33:41,503 --> 00:33:44,256
- Let's take this one step at a time, okay?
- Absolutely.

580
00:34:24,379 --> 00:34:25,422
Abbott.

581
00:34:29,718 --> 00:34:30,761
Let's get in the air, yeah?

582
00:34:31,595 --> 00:34:33,847
Uh, I just need a couple more minutes.
Let me check one more last thing.

583
00:34:34,806 --> 00:34:36,183
When are you meeting up
with your man?

584
00:34:36,433 --> 00:34:38,602
I'm gonna call him
as soon as we get out of state.

585
00:34:53,950 --> 00:34:55,035
Love you, baby.

586
00:35:04,294 --> 00:35:05,545
Hey, there, Missy.

587
00:35:08,882 --> 00:35:10,675
- What were you doing?
- Nothing.

588
00:35:11,426 --> 00:35:12,761
Hendricks, grab your gun.

589
00:35:19,351 --> 00:35:20,560
What's your game?

590
00:35:23,230 --> 00:35:24,272
What do you need a gun for?

591
00:35:24,731 --> 00:35:26,483
I have no idea
what you're talking about.

592
00:35:26,900 --> 00:35:28,026
Is that right?

593
00:35:29,611 --> 00:35:32,906
- "Where'd she come from anyway?"
- "She was my celly. I told you."

594
00:35:33,448 --> 00:35:35,784
- "So why's she need a gun?"
- "How should I know?"

595
00:35:36,535 --> 00:35:37,869
I don't like this.

596
00:35:38,578 --> 00:35:40,539
- I do not like this.
- Baby.

597
00:35:41,665 --> 00:35:42,707
"Don't baby me."

598
00:35:43,416 --> 00:35:45,794
"She was going for the gun.
She thinks she's slick."

599
00:35:46,086 --> 00:35:47,712
"She thinks she's gonna
put one over on us."

600
00:35:47,963 --> 00:35:49,005
"So, what are we gonna do?"

601
00:35:49,381 --> 00:35:51,800
"What? You want me to draw you a
sketch? You know what."

602
00:35:52,592 --> 00:35:54,094
"Just let me think
a second, okay?"

603
00:35:55,178 --> 00:35:58,473
"This isn't the time for thinking.
It's time for action."

604
00:36:08,900 --> 00:36:10,277
Hey. We're ready to go.

605
00:36:11,903 --> 00:36:14,406
Not until we deal with her.
Sure as hell can't leave her behind.

606
00:36:14,614 --> 00:36:15,782
She knows what our plans are.

607
00:36:17,576 --> 00:36:19,035
Look, that only leaves
one option.

608
00:36:24,165 --> 00:36:26,001
She's good people.
Just make it quick.

609
00:36:28,295 --> 00:36:29,337
"Excuse me."

610
00:36:32,215 --> 00:36:35,468
Patrick Jane, FBI.
Drop your weapons. You're coming with me.

611
00:36:47,286 --> 00:36:50,122
Got this place
surrounded with snipers.

612
00:36:51,665 --> 00:36:54,668
You put your guns down right now, you walk
out of here alive. You hear that?

613
00:36:55,878 --> 00:36:57,379
- You're lying.
- Oh, really?

614
00:36:57,505 --> 00:37:01,967
You think I'd walk in here
unarmed with no cover, do you?

615
00:37:02,635 --> 00:37:04,803
Well, I know you
from somewhere.

616
00:37:05,513 --> 00:37:08,849
Cole, there's a sniper in that tree
over there. I can see his glass.

617
00:37:11,310 --> 00:37:12,895
No one has to die, not today.

618
00:37:13,562 --> 00:37:15,314
I know you.
What's he doing here?

619
00:37:15,773 --> 00:37:17,441
- Who is he?
- It's her boyfriend!

620
00:37:17,566 --> 00:37:19,109
I saw him at the jail.
He's a con artist.

621
00:37:19,235 --> 00:37:21,028
It's some kind of trick.
What the hell's going on?

622
00:37:27,451 --> 00:37:28,494
Well, here we are.

623
00:37:32,748 --> 00:37:34,500
You walked out here
to face us by yourself

624
00:37:34,708 --> 00:37:36,710
with nothing but a rearview
mirror for a backup?

625
00:37:37,127 --> 00:37:38,170
Worth a shot.

626
00:37:39,672 --> 00:37:41,757
Sorry, I, I couldn't
think of anything else.

627
00:37:42,383 --> 00:37:43,425
It's okay.

628
00:37:49,348 --> 00:37:50,891
- "FBI!"
- Drop your weapon right now!

629
00:37:51,016 --> 00:37:52,351
- Don't move.
- Put your gun down.

630
00:37:52,476 --> 00:37:53,644
- Freeze.
- Get down.

631
00:37:53,769 --> 00:37:55,229
Get on your knees!
Put your hands on your hand!

632
00:37:56,063 --> 00:37:57,982
- Hands where I can see them!
- Do it now!

633
00:37:58,566 --> 00:38:00,150
- That's an order! Now!
- Cuff her, Vega.

634
00:38:00,276 --> 00:38:01,694
- Okay. Okay.
- Yes, sir.

635
00:38:02,486 --> 00:38:04,780
Oh, I'm so glad
you decided to catch up.

636
00:38:05,197 --> 00:38:07,074
- You dropped this.
- Thank you.

637
00:38:08,284 --> 00:38:09,910
- Hey.
- Hey.

638
00:38:10,327 --> 00:38:11,370
Here we are.

639
00:38:20,921 --> 00:38:21,964
I know what you want.

640
00:38:22,756 --> 00:38:23,799
You want my contacts.

641
00:38:24,717 --> 00:38:26,760
International smugglers.
I can give them to you.

642
00:38:27,970 --> 00:38:30,806
Lots of them.
Names, locations.

643
00:38:31,140 --> 00:38:33,267
Hell, I will tell you
what their favorite foods are.

644
00:38:34,143 --> 00:38:36,270
But first,
what are you gonna give me?

645
00:38:36,562 --> 00:38:39,064
You give us everything
and we don't charge Marie

646
00:38:39,189 --> 00:38:41,108
as an accessory
to the murder you committed.

647
00:38:41,442 --> 00:38:43,652
She'll get out, have a chance
to have some kind of life.

648
00:38:43,861 --> 00:38:44,903
You kidding me?

649
00:38:45,237 --> 00:38:48,824
You think that I'm gonna spend the
only coin I got on that crazy bitch?

650
00:38:49,700 --> 00:38:51,243
You're gonna have to do
something for me.

651
00:38:51,368 --> 00:38:52,911
You killed a man today for
no reason at all

652
00:38:53,037 --> 00:38:55,456
you did it on tape and you did it
in front of an FBI agent.

653
00:38:55,956 --> 00:38:57,791
No death penalty,
that's the deal.

654
00:38:58,334 --> 00:39:01,837
Now, you're gonna die in jail
just not gonna be for a while is all.

655
00:39:02,421 --> 00:39:03,464
Take it or leave it.

656
00:39:08,510 --> 00:39:09,553
I'll take it.

657
00:39:16,685 --> 00:39:18,896
Yes. We can work with this.

658
00:39:19,188 --> 00:39:20,898
- "Read through this, please."
- We'll send you a transcript

659
00:39:21,023 --> 00:39:22,399
as soon as he's done signing.

660
00:39:25,819 --> 00:39:27,488
Agent Cho,
did he agree to talk?

661
00:39:28,238 --> 00:39:30,199
Yeah. You did good today.

662
00:39:31,742 --> 00:39:34,078
Agent Cho, sir,
may I say something?

663
00:39:36,288 --> 00:39:38,332
You don't have to call me
sir or agent.

664
00:39:40,459 --> 00:39:41,752
I've been observing your work

665
00:39:42,002 --> 00:39:44,171
and I admire the way
you carry yourself on the job.

666
00:39:44,880 --> 00:39:48,550
This place is a little bit crazy
but you make sense to me.

667
00:39:49,468 --> 00:39:50,511
Okay.

668
00:39:51,220 --> 00:39:53,305
I would welcome the opportunity
to work with you more

669
00:39:53,639 --> 00:39:55,766
learn how you do things,
get some pointers.

670
00:39:57,059 --> 00:39:58,519
I don't know.
I'll have to think about it.

671
00:39:59,895 --> 00:40:02,606
Oh. Oh, okay. Sounds good.
Thank you.

672
00:40:14,076 --> 00:40:15,411
- Jane.
- Yeah?

673
00:40:15,786 --> 00:40:18,539
Just talked to Abbott. The CIA got in
touch with him about one of the names

674
00:40:18,664 --> 00:40:20,124
that Cole gave up,
some smuggler.

675
00:40:20,499 --> 00:40:22,042
Oh, that's great.
That's progress.

676
00:40:22,167 --> 00:40:24,169
Well, the Agency squeezed Cole
for everything they could get

677
00:40:24,294 --> 00:40:26,046
associates, habits,
personal life.

678
00:40:26,338 --> 00:40:27,673
Well, what does that
got to do with us?

679
00:40:28,090 --> 00:40:29,508
Turns out we know
the smuggler's girlfriend.

680
00:40:29,675 --> 00:40:31,760
- Well, you do.
- I do?

